  (text "ADS1115 #1 (0x48): A0-A1 differential = shunt (current, +-256 mV range), A2-A3 differential = cell voltage / 2 (Kelvin, +-2.048 V range)."
    (at 25 178.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 22117702-0e1e-4fc7-8890-a8440d8e41ae))
  (text "ADS1115 #2 (0x49): four NTC channels (10k B3950, 10k pull-up): cell surface, pocket air, load heatsink, Peltier hot side."
    (at 25 182.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 3bdbf0fb-7d9c-461b-809f-193029058a6d))
  (text "V_FAST: cell voltage / 2 for the Blue Pill internal ADC (pulse capture at ~1 kHz). It is ground-referenced, so subtract I x shunt in software."
    (at 25 187.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 2254880a-103d-4fef-8bc3-9707ae82e521))
  (text "Divider resistors R503/R504 should be 0.1 % 25 ppm, or calibrate against a DMM. ADS1115 modules plug into 1x10 female headers."
    (at 25 191.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 1e055127-d281-4cb9-837c-438c3631e583))  (text "v0.3 REVIEW NOTES - explained in docs/SCHEMATIC_GUIDE.md section 5; checklist with comment columns in docs/SCHEMATIC_REVIEW.md"
    (at 25 200.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5) bold)
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 98c0b7bf-bdef-4806-a314-b14da8404ffc))
  (text "How it works: U501 A0-A1 = shunt (0.8 mA/bit), A2-A3 = cell voltage / 2 between the Kelvin wires. U502 = 4 NTCs (10k pull-up, B3950)."
    (at 25 205.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid b75971bf-dfa5-45f4-989d-25fd94e87bdd))
  (text "V_FAST (R510/R511) -> PA1 for fast pulses (R0); referenced to GND, so subtract I x R_shunt."
    (at 25 210.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 0edc1437-ad87-45a4-b10c-eeddaef1af9f))
  (text "CHECK M-02: R503/R504 0.1 %.  M-04: the SENSE_P dividers drain ~0.9 mA from the cell and back-power unpowered ICs when the bench is off."
    (at 25 214.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid d6a16784-1d7d-4be4-b266-9ab39951eebb))
)
